1 Create a Git Repository
mkdir git-practical
cd git-practical
git init
git status

2 Create a File and Track Changes
cd git-practical
echo "Welcome to Git and GitHub" > message.txt
git status
git add message.txt
git status

3 Commit Changes to the Repository
cd git-practical
echo "First Git commit" > commit-demo.txt
git add commit-demo.txt
git commit -m "Add first commit demo"
git log --oneline

4 View Commit History
cd git-practical
git log
git log --oneline

5 Undo Changes Using Git Commands
cd git-practical
echo "Original content" > undo-demo.txt
git add undo-demo.txt
git commit -m "Add original content"
echo "Unwanted change" > undo-demo.txt
git restore undo-demo.txt
cat undo-demo.txt
git status

6 Create, Switch, and Delete a Branch
cd git-practical
git branch
git branch feature-demo
git switch feature-demo
git branch
git switch main
git branch -d feature-demo
git branch

7 Resolve a Merge Conflict
cd git-practical
echo "Welcome to Git" > conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m "Add conflict demo file"

git switch -c feature-conflict
echo "Feature branch content" > conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m "Update file in feature branch"

git switch main
echo "Main branch content" > conflict-demo.txt
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m "Update file in main branch"

git merge feature-conflict
If a conflict occurs, edit conflict-demo.txt and remove the conflict markers (<<<<<<<, =======, >>>>>>>). Keep the content you want, then run:
git add conflict-demo.txt
git commit -m "Resolve merge conflict"
cat conflict-demo.txt
git status

8 Store and Restore Changes Using Git Stash
cd git-practical
echo "Original content" > notes.txt
git add notes.txt
git commit -m "Add original notes"

echo "Temporary work" >> notes.txt
git stash push -m "Save temporary work"
git status
git stash pop
cat notes.txt

9 Configure a Remote Repository
cd /workspaces/git-practical
git remote -v
If origin is not configured, add it:
git remote add origin https://github.com/anandajothi-2007/git-practical.git
git remote -v
If origin already exists, do not add it again.

10 Clone, Push, and Pull Changes
Use a different folder name if git-practical already exists in your current directory.
cd /workspaces
git clone https://github.com/anandajothi-2007/git-practical.git
cd git-practical
echo "Push and pull practical" > push-pull-demo.txt
git add push-pull-demo.txt
git commit -m "Add push pull demo"
git push origin main
git pull origin main
cat push-pull-demo.txt

11 Fork a Repository and Create a Pull Request
This exercise was performed using the GitHub website, so terminal commands are not required. The equivalent command to clone your fork is:
git clone https://github.com/anandajothi-2007/Hello-World.git
cd Hello-World
git status

12 Collaborative Editing with Multiple Contributors
cd /workspaces/git-practical
echo "Collaborative editing practical - Exercise 12" > collaboration.txt
git add collaboration.txt
git commit -m "Add collaborative editing exercise"
git push origin main
After the collaborator commits and pushes their contribution, run:
git pull origin main
cat collaboration.txt
git log --oneline -5

